# core/data/talk/grammar/en/warm_comfort.tlk - more replies to comfort, encouragement and
# sympathy (owner: TK; T5b package T5B-WARM). The light kind: a bad day, a nerve, a grumble.
# Real grief and distress have their own sincere banks (grief.tlk, safety.tlk): nothing here
# jokes about loss, and no line here makes light of someone being truly hurt. No register
# word, no filler that needs a guard the rule lacks. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.

# ---- COMFORT: thank -------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.comfort.w_thank act: thank
  "Thank you. I didn't know how much I needed that."
  "That's really kind. I feel a little lighter."
  "Thanks for sitting with me. It helps. A lot, actually."
  "You're good at this. Don't tell anyone, they'll all line up."
  "Okay, deep breath. {.}Better. Thank you."
  "I was a mess a minute ago. Now I'm a smaller mess."
  "That's nice of you. I'm keeping it somewhere safe."
  "Thanks. I think the cloud is moving off."
  "You always say the right thing. Even when you say nothing."
  "That helped. A warm drink would help more, but this is great."
  "Thank you. I'm going to try believing that."
  "Yeah. Yeah, okay. Thanks for the hand."
  "I feel heard. It's a strange feeling. I like it."
  "My chest feels less tight. That's all you."
  "Thanks. You make a good blanket."
@rule core.comfort.w_thank_polite guard: polite act: thank
  "That's very thoughtful of you. I'm grateful."
  "You are kind to say so. It truly helps."
  "Thank you for your patience with me. It means a lot."
@rule core.comfort.w_thank_flat guard: flat act: thank
  "Thanks. {.}I feel it. It's just very quiet in here."
  "Okay. That helped. I'm saying it flat, but I mean it."
  "Huh. That worked. Thanks."
@rule core.comfort.w_thank_blunt guard: blunt act: thank
  "Fine. That helped. Don't gloat."
  "Thanks. I hate that it worked."
  "Yeah, okay, thanks. Now never mention it."
@rule core.comfort.w_thank_elder guard: elder act: thank
  "Bless you, dear. I've had worse days, but not many."
  "That's good of you. Kindness keeps an old heart ticking."
  "Thanks, dear. A good talk is better than a pill."
@rule core.comfort.w_thank_teen guard: teen&!kid_speaker act: thank
  "Okay. Thanks. I didn't think anyone would get it."
  "That's, like, actually helpful. Don't make it weird."
  "Thanks. I'm fine. Better, anyway, mostly."
@rule core.comfort.w_thank_sad guard: mood=sad act: thank
  "Thank you. I'm still sad, but less alone about it."
  "I'm not okay yet. But it helps that you're here."
  "That means a lot. I'm just going to sit here a bit."
@rule core.comfort.w_thank_tired guard: mood=tired act: thank
  "Thanks. I'm so tired. But you made it easier."
  "Mm. That's nice. I could fall asleep on that."
@rule core.comfort.w_thank_scared guard: mood=scared act: thank
  "Thanks. I'm still jumpy, but I feel braver with you here."
  "Okay. Breathing. Thank you for staying."
@rule core.comfort.w_thank_friend guard: rel=friend act: thank
  "That's why you're my friend. You just show up."
  "I'm lucky to have you. Seriously. Thank you."
@rule core.comfort.w_thank_best guard: rel=best act: thank
  "I'd be lost without you. Please don't leave."
  "You always know. How do you always know?"
@rule core.comfort.w_thank_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: thank
  "Thank you. I feel better. Can I have a cookie now?"
  "Okay. I'll stop crying now. Thanks for the hug-words."
  "You're nice. I like it when you're nice."
  "Thanks. My tummy stopped feeling funny."
@rule core.comfort.w_thank_night guard: night act: thank
  "Thanks. Things always feel bigger at night. You made it smaller."
  "That's kind. I'll sleep better now. Maybe."

# ---- COMFORT: answer, complain, joke ---------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.comfort.w_answer act: answer
  "It's just been a lot lately. Everything at once."
  "I don't know. I woke up on the wrong side of everything."
  "Mostly I'm worried I'm not good enough. Silly, right?"
  "It's nothing big. Lots of small things in a pile."
  "I'm tired in a way sleep can't fix. You know?"
  "Things piled up. I just need a minute. And a snack."
  "I keep thinking I forgot something. I don't know what."
  "It'll pass. It always does. I just wish it passed faster."
@rule core.comfort.w_answer_flat guard: flat act: answer
  "It's fine. I'm fine. {.}It's a quiet kind of not fine."
  "Nothing's wrong. I just feel grey. Like a Monday."
@rule core.comfort.w_answer_blunt guard: blunt act: answer
  "Bad day. That's it. Don't fuss."
  "I'm in a mood. Give it an hour. Bring cake."
@rule core.comfort.w_answer_slow guard: slow act: answer
  "I'm okay. {.}I think. Give me a moment to check."
  "It's a slow, heavy sort of day. I'll get through it."
@rule core.comfort.w_answer_elder guard: elder act: answer
  "Oh, my bones ache and my mind drifts. It's the weather."
  "I miss how it used to be. That's all. It's just a feeling."
@rule core.comfort.w_answer_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: answer
  "Somebody took my crayon and didn't say sorry."
  "I'm sad because it's raining and I can't go out."
  "I had a bad dream. There was a really big spoon."
@rule core.comfort.w_complain act: complain
  "Don't be nice to me, I'll cry. Ugh. Too late."
  "I'm fine! I just really, really hate everything right now."
  "It's not fair. None of it. I want a refund."
  "Why is the world like this? Who do I talk to?"
  "I was doing okay until you asked. Now I'm mad about it."
  "Everything's annoying. Even the nice things are annoying."
@rule core.comfort.w_joke act: joke
  "Don't be nice, I might get used to it. Then what?"
  "My mood bar went from red to a slightly softer red."
  "You're like a big, warm sandwich. Say another kind thing."
  "Keep talking like that and I'll start a fan club."
  "I'm weeping, but in a cool, controlled way."
  "I was going to feel sorry for myself. You ruined my schedule."
@rule core.comfort.w_joke_quirky guard: quirky act: joke
  "My feelings are in a pocket. I'll go find them."
  "It's okay. I put my worries in the fridge. They'll keep."

# ---- ENCOURAGE: thank -----------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.encourage.w_thank act: thank
  "You believe in me? Huh. Then I'd better believe too."
  "Thanks. I needed someone to say that out loud."
  "Okay! I'll give it a go. A real go, with effort."
  "That's the push I wanted. A gentle push. Not a shove."
  "You're right. I can do hard things. I did one before breakfast."
  "I like how you say that. Like it's already true."
  "Thanks, coach. Do I get a whistle?"
  "Well, now I have to try. You've got me all inspired."
  "That actually helps. I'll take it with me."
  "Good point. Worst case, I try again tomorrow."
  "Okay, deep breath. {.}Here I go. Thank you."
  "Thanks for having my back. It's a good back. Hard to find."
@rule core.encourage.w_thank_polite guard: polite act: thank
  "How encouraging of you. I'll do my best."
  "You are very kind to say so. I shall try."
@rule core.encourage.w_thank_flat guard: flat act: thank
  "Okay. I'll try. {.}That's me being fired up."
  "Sure. Thanks. I'll go be brave now, quietly."
@rule core.encourage.w_thank_blunt guard: blunt act: thank
  "Fine. I'll do it. But if it goes badly, you're blamed."
  "Yeah, okay. You've convinced me. Don't get smug."
@rule core.encourage.w_thank_loud guard: loud act: thank
  "YES! I'm doing it. Watch me, I'm so ready."
  "You're right! I'm going to be AMAZING at this!"
@rule core.encourage.w_thank_elder guard: elder act: thank
  "Well, I did a lot of things at your age. Some on purpose."
  "Thank you, dear. A little courage goes a long way at my age."
@rule core.encourage.w_thank_teen guard: teen&!kid_speaker act: thank
  "Okay, that actually helped. I'll go for it. Maybe."
  "Thanks. Everyone else just says, like, whatever. You mean it."
@rule core.encourage.w_thank_tired guard: mood=tired act: thank
  "Thanks. I'll do it after a nap. A short, brave nap."
  "Okay, I'm doing it. Slowly, so don't watch."
@rule core.encourage.w_thank_scared guard: mood=scared act: thank
  "I'm scared, but I'll try anyway. That counts, right?"
  "Okay. My knees are knocking, but I'm going."
@rule core.encourage.w_thank_friend guard: rel=friend act: thank
  "You always cheer me on. I'll cheer you on next time."
  "With a friend like you, how can I lose? Easily, but still."
@rule core.encourage.w_thank_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: thank
  "Okay! I'll be brave. Super brave, or medium brave."
  "Thanks! I'll try so hard I'll go red in the face!"
  "You really think I can? Then I really can!"

# ---- ENCOURAGE: yes, joke, complain ----------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.encourage.w_yes act: yes
  "Yes! You're right, let's do it. Right after this."
  "Yes. I'm going to do it. For real this time."
  "Okay, fine, yes, I'll do it. Stop being so persuasive."
  "Right, no more excuses. Okay, one more excuse. Done."
  "You're right. I'm ready. Mostly ready."
  "Yes! A new me starts today. Probably after lunch."
@rule core.encourage.w_yes_blunt guard: blunt act: yes
  "Fine, yes, I'm doing it. Quit staring."
  "Fair. I'll go. Don't clap yet."
@rule core.encourage.w_yes_flat guard: flat act: yes
  "Yes. {.}Consider me emotionally invested."
  "Okay. I'll do it. That's my excited voice."
@rule core.encourage.w_joke act: joke
  "Next you'll say I'm a winner. I'll go lie down."
  "Keep going, that was almost a pep talk."
  "I'd get up and do it, but my chair's so loyal."
  "Great speech. Do you take requests? My request is again."
  "You should write cards. I'd buy one. With glitter."
  "I'm so motivated, I'm going to plan to plan."
  "That was inspiring. I'm going to need to sit down."
@rule core.encourage.w_complain act: complain
  "Easy for you to say. You're not the one doing it."
  "I don't want to be brave. I want a nap and a donut."
  "That's a lot of pressure. Can I get a smaller pep talk?"
  "Don't say 'you can do it.' It sounds like a threat."
  "I'm trying! I'm just not very good at trying."

# ---- SYMPATHIZE: thank ----------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.sympathize.w_thank act: thank
  "Thank you. It's nice not to be the only one who sees it."
  "That's kind. Most people just say oh well."
  "I appreciate that. It helps to be understood."
  "Thanks for getting it. I mean that."
  "You're a good listener. I'm going to tell everyone."
  "That's nice of you to say. It really is."
  "Thanks. I didn't want advice. I wanted exactly that."
  "Aw. You get me. Two points for you."
  "Thanks. It's been a rough stretch, and that helps."
  "You know what? That made me feel less silly about it."
@rule core.sympathize.w_thank_polite guard: polite act: thank
  "You are most understanding. Thank you."
  "That's very considerate of you. I'm touched."
@rule core.sympathize.w_thank_flat guard: flat act: thank
  "Thanks. {.}I wasn't expecting someone to get it."
  "Noted. And appreciated. I'm just saying it plain."
@rule core.sympathize.w_thank_blunt guard: blunt act: thank
  "Yeah. Thanks. Most people don't bother."
  "Fine. That was nice. Don't tell anyone."
@rule core.sympathize.w_thank_elder guard: elder act: thank
  "Thank you, dear. Not many listen to an old one."
  "That's sweet. You're young, but you've got a good heart."
@rule core.sympathize.w_thank_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: thank
  "Thanks for being nice about it. It was a big deal."
  "I feel less sad now. You said sorry the right way."
@rule core.sympathize.w_thank_sad guard: mood=sad act: thank
  "Thanks. It really is hard right now. It helps to hear that."
  "That's kind. I'm trying to stay strong. It's okay to wobble."
@rule core.sympathize.w_thank_friend guard: rel=friend act: thank
  "Thanks, friend. You always get the whole story."
  "You're a good friend. Seriously."

# ---- SYMPATHIZE: complain, agree, joke ------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.sympathize.w_complain act: complain
  "It's just so unfair. I did everything right!"
  "Right? And then they act like it's my fault. Unbelievable."
  "Ugh, exactly. I could go on all day. Shall I?"
  "Thank you! And that's not even the worst part."
  "I know! It never ends. I'm going to scream into a pillow."
  "It's the little things that get me. And the big things."
@rule core.sympathize.w_complain_blunt guard: blunt act: complain
  "Exactly. It stinks. All of it."
  "Yeah, it's garbage. Total garbage. Say it with me."
@rule core.sympathize.w_agree act: agree
  "Yes. Exactly. You understand."
  "That's what I've been saying. Nobody listens."
  "Right? It's not just me. Thank goodness."
  "Yep. It is what it is. But it is a lot."
  "I'd say it better, but you nailed it."
  "True. Thanks for saying so. It's nice to be agreed with."
@rule core.sympathize.w_joke act: joke
  "Thanks for the sympathy. I'll put it in my pocket with my feelings."
  "That's nice. Sympathy is my second favourite snack."
  "I accept this sympathy. Please send it in a card next time."
  "You'd make a good pillow. A sympathetic pillow."
  "Is it weird that I'm enjoying being pitied? A bit?"
  "My problems and I thank you. They feel seen."
@rule core.sympathize.w_joke_quirky guard: quirky act: joke
  "Sympathy accepted! I'll pay you in marbles."
  "It's all right. I've been rained on by worse. Tuesday."
